OL,3,GNEWSAIsolation of stroke tackled in
OL,4,Acharity support group
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe husband of a stroke survivor has
OL,7,Ftold how a communications support group
OL,8,Fhas provided a "lifeline" for his wife.
OL,10,FAndrew Ingrouille's wife Bridget had a
OL,11,Fstroke three years ago and now has
OL,12,Faphasia, meaning she can no longer read
OL,13,For write and her speech is limited.
OL,15,FAndrew said "it was devastating,"
OL,16,Fadding "one day you're going through
OL,17,Flife normally... and suddenly your
OL,18,Fwhole world collapses".
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
